# T-460: russh 0.65.0's reading of a global request's reply in place of the
# patch's (vendor/patches/russh/0001-reply-data.patch taken out of
# vendor/russh, its other patches kept): a failure with 15 bytes after the
# default keepalive ends the connection again, so the quiet session against
# the stand-in of x/crypto/ssh must fail. Since T-664 podssh calls a method of
# a later patch (0003), so the published crate in the copy's place no longer
# builds; the patch 0001 taken out is the published reading. On the runner,
# not in the build image: the harness starts containers of its own (Go's
# image, Alpine's).
ENTRY=T-460
GROUP=host-gossh
EXPECT='^FAIL +go-ssh\.quiet\.failure\.default '
RUN='cargo build --locked -p podssh-cli && PODSSH_ENGINE=docker sh scripts/interop-go-ssh.sh "$PWD/target/debug/podssh"'
LIMIT=2400
